# ---- Entries (schema:Comment; text + attribution) ----

<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-decision-05> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Session handling moves into core: consumers need no session watching at all. Core fetches the profile from its own session and builds the search index on first demand (zero-arg os.buildSearchIndex() — the profile parameter is dropped, core resolves it itself), keeps it warm until logout, and empties held references in place on logout. Angelo's reasoning: core should keep the index up to date but only if it is needed — no index for consumers that never ask, and core-managed freshness once one does. Login needs no handling (pos-app resolves only after OIDC redirect/session restore completes, so consumers mount already logged in); logout is handled by core's existing session tap — which must additionally empty the cached instance in place, not only drop the reference (drafted as task-07). The elements-side session watch (pos-navigation pattern) and the consumer-side profile fetch/build call both become unnecessary; the earlier keep-explicit-build choice is thereby superseded." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T20:14:23Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-scope-05> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "With decision-05 the mention flow reduces to: RichEditor takes os: PodOS; mention(os) calls os.buildSearchIndex() (zero-arg demand API, no session logic in the extension) and maps refs to {id, label} via os.store.get(ref).label(); pos-markdown-document passes os through; core owns build-on-demand and logout clearing (task-07)." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T20:14:23Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-goal-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Core owns the search-index lifecycle end to end: os.buildSearchIndex() (zero-arg) builds on first demand (profile fetched from core's own session), stays warm until logout, and on logout empties the cached instance in place so that references already held by consumers see the cleared index instead of serving the previous user's data. After a re-login the next call is a cache miss and rebuilds." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T20:14:23Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-scope-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "SearchGateway: SearchIndex.clear() currently only drops the cached reference (this.cached = undefined) — held references keep serving stale data. Make the logout path empty the cached instance in place (call SearchIndex.clear() on the instance) so consumers holding a reference see an empty index immediately. Re-login triggers a fresh build (cache miss)." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T20:14:23Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-context-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Spun out of task-05's planning (2026-10-14): Angelo argued the index should not be built when nobody uses it, but once a consumer exists core should manage it — including emptying held references on logout, which SearchGateway.clear() does not do today (it only drops the cache; pos-navigation papers over the gap with its own session watch + in-place clear). Draft status: needs planning through (logged-out semantics of the demand API, deprecation of buildSearchIndex, consumer migration order) before implementation. PLANNED THROUGH (2026-10-15): logged-out resolves empty & uncached, gateway owns the lifecycle, task-07 lands before task-05 (pos-navigation call-site migrated, session-watch removal deferred to task-05), in-place empty on every session change." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T20:14:23Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-scope-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "SearchGateway takes session + ProfileGateway injected (constructor grows); its buildSearchIndex() becomes zero-arg and resolves the profile itself: read webId from the session, fetchProfile(webId), build + cache as today. PodOS reduces to a thin delegator os.buildSearchIndex() -> searchGateway.buildSearchIndex(). The gateway becomes the single owner of the whole search lifecycle (demand-build, cache, rebuild-on-write, logout-clear). Placement trade-off (LLM): rejected (a) PodOS-orchestrates — smaller diff but PodOS accumulates orchestration logic, and (b) a separate SearchIndexService — cleanest separation but one more object for a single consumer (YAGNI)." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-15T06:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-scope-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Logged-out semantics (Angelo chose 'resolve empty', 2026-10-15): a zero-arg call while logged out resolves immediately with a FRESH empty SearchIndex (new SearchIndex([])) that is NOT cached — the next call after login is a cache miss and builds. This prevents pinning a consumer to an empty index forever. Logged-in calls resolve the profile from the session (fetchProfile) and build + cache as today. Rejected (LLM): wait-for-next-login (would block a consumer until login; the mention menu must render without awaiting the index) and reject-with-error (would force session handling back into consumers)." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-15T06:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-scope-04> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Consumer migration deferred (task ordering confirmed 2026-10-15): pos-navigation keeps its session watch and its buildSearchIndex(session.state.profile) call initially; the one-line call-site change to the zero-arg call happens in task-07 (signature is breaking), but the session-watch removal is deferred to task-05's implementation. The mention extension (task-05) is designed against the zero-arg API from the start. The elements-side session store / pos-app profile population stays untouched: it still fills sessionStore.state.profile for other consumers (pos-make-findable uses it); core's gateway reads the webId from its own core session, not from the elements store." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-15T06:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-decision-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Placement: the SearchGateway owns the full search lifecycle (session + ProfileGateway injected into its constructor, buildSearchIndex() zero-arg); PodOS becomes a thin delegator. Angelo: 'PodOS index should not contain any logic at best. but not sure if the gateway is the right place' (chose gateway-owns fully, 2026-10-15)." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-15T06:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-decision-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Logged-out call resolves empty immediately — no waiting for the next login, no error (Angelo chose 'resolve empty', 2026-10-15)." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-15T06:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-decision-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "In-place empty fires on EVERY session change, not only on the logout transition (Angelo chose 'every session change', 2026-10-15). Implementation (LLM): SearchGateway.clear() becomes 'empty held instance in place, then drop the reference' — this.cached?.clear(); this.cached = undefined; no transition detection (isLoggedIn true->false check) — the tap already fires on every change and login/switch is covered by rebuild-on-demand (cache miss after clear)." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-15T06:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-decision-04> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Ordering: task-07 lands before task-05; pos-navigation migrates its call site to the zero-arg call in task-07, while removing its session watch is deferred to task-05 (Angelo, 2026-10-15)." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-15T06:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-decision-05> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "The demand API keeps the existing name os.buildSearchIndex() — signature loses the profile parameter (no deprecation, no new name): every consumer call site (pos-navigation, mention extension) migrates to the zero-arg call." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-15T06:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-verification-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Unit tests (SearchGateway.spec, fake Store + fake session): buildSearchIndex() zero-arg while logged out -> resolves fresh empty SearchIndex (search() empty), NOT cached (a later logged-in call builds — fetchAll called); while logged in -> fetchProfile called with session webId, index cached (same instance on repeat), fetchAll once; logout after build -> held instance is empty in place (search() empty on the SAME reference) and cache dropped (next call rebuilds). pos-navigation suite stays green with the one-line call-site change; PodOs.spec 'clears the cached search index when the session changes' extended to assert the in-place empty on held references." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-15T06:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-note-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Cycle 1 process (2026-10-15, logged while working): the zero-arg signature is breaking, so cycle 1 necessarily migrated every call site in the same cycle to keep the package compiling — PodOS became a thin zero-arg delegator and SearchGateway.integration.spec.ts (its only buildSearchIndex call) plus PodOs.spec.ts moved to zero-arg calls; pos-navigation keeps its session watch and its profile-arg call untouched per scope-04 (its elements suite cannot run without a core build; task-05 removes the watch). Verification entry followed exactly, in this order: (1) logged-out resolves fresh empty index, (2) logged-in fetchProfile with session webId + cache (same instance on repeat), (3) session tap empty held instance in place. Mid-cycle correction: the first cut constructed a ProfileGateway inside SearchGateway, which broke the spec\'s fake stores (ProfileGateway needs store.fetch + profileQuery); scope-02 already prescribed constructor injection — switched to injecting ProfileGateway, and the fakes turned clean again. Pre-existing detail surfaced by the fake store: PodOs.spec\'s old cache test passed a profile even though the pod-level test only verifies cache invalidation on session change." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-15T06:18:53Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-note-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "PodOs.spec cycle-1 note: the session tap now calls SearchGateway.clear() on EVERY session emission — not only on logout transitions. The existing test (\'clears the cached search index when the session changes\') asserts rebuild after any session change, which stays correct under decision-03; the in-place-empty assertion on held references is added with the tap change in the next cycle (kept out of cycle 1 to keep each commit one green slice)." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-15T06:18:53Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-note-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Wallaby process note (2026-10-15): two wallaby server instances were observed (repo-root auto-detect vs core/); the core/ session occasionally served stale instrumented copies right after a file was saved — reported tests referenced code that was no longer on disk (ReferenceError inside the CURRENT file content). A no-op touch of the changed file forced a re-instrumentation and the live state matched reality again. There is no wallaby.js config in the repo; the CLI auto-detects per working directory (core/ and elements/ are the two session roots used by the TDD loop)." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-15T06:18:53Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-note-04> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "rdf_patch process note (2026-10-15): the tool cannot round-trip this plan file — its relative IRIs (<../plan-ontology.ttl#>, <#...>) get rewritten to absolute file:// URIs inside a GRAPH block it emits, which breaks the document (verified: rdf_validate then failed to parse). Plan writes therefore use targeted text edits + rdf_validate (with BASE-prefixed copies to sidestep the file:// artifact) instead of rdf_patch; the file was restored from git once after the first mangled patch. This affects every plan write, not just this task." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-15T06:18:53Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-note-05> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Cycle 2 process (2026-10-15): the in-place-empty test was first written tautologically (held reference built while logged out) and passed by construction; rewritten to build a NON-empty cached index with real profile + label-index documents (mockTurtleDocument in PodOs.spec, empty profile doc + one labelled item), so the held reference carries alice\'s item across the session change. Red was proven with a standalone probe against the built package (before=1, after=1) because the PodOs-level suite could not express the failure without the fixture. One extra mock (profile/card#me alias) noted: Store.fetch normalizes fragment URIs to their document URI, only the document URL is fetched." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-15T06:27:30Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-07-core-searchindex-demand-api-note-06> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Cycle 3 process (2026-10-15): the elements workspace typecheck (tsc --noEmit) fails on MAIN with ~211 pre-existing errors (loose strictness: TS2564 initializers, TS2322/TS7031 etc.) — it is not wired into the repo-level typecheck script (only core/contacts have one), so it is not a gate; verified the pos-navigation call-site error (TS2554) was the only delta from this task\'s change by stashing the migrated file. The one-line migration to the zero-arg call landed in cycle 2 per decision-04; the session watch stays per scope-04. Cycle-3 red turned out to be a test bug (no re-login emission after the logged-out call), not an implementation gap — the implementation already covered the chain, proven by a standalone probe (logged-out -> alice -> logout -> bob rebuilds correctly); the test was fixed and the single clear() line kept. Also added the verification entry\'s fetchProfile-with-webId assertion to the built-twice test (test-only hardening, verified green before commit)." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-15T06:27:30Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-goal-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "The RichEditor mention menu gets its suggestions from the search index and the store instead of hardcoded items: items(query) maps searchIndex.search(query) refs via os.store.get(ref) Things to [{id, label}]. The mention extension is re-enabled and its 3 skipped tests restored — with this task the plan goal (mentions backed by label search, same as pos-navigation) is reached.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T19:26:26Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-note-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "First implementation attempt of the provider glue in pos-markdown-document.tsx was committed (3fe3ba0a) and then reverted (f5052c1f): Angelo rejected the placement. All the os-backed suggestion logic (obtaining os, building the search index, session watch, ref→label lookup) must live inside the mention extension instead; the component reduces to wiring. Kept from the reverted attempt: the seam tests (mention() items delegation in index.spec.ts, RichEditor constructor provider arg) and the non-blocking lazy-provider design (provider resolves to [] until the index is available; rendering never awaits os)." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T20:07:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-decision-04> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Os-backed logic lives in the mention extension, not in the markdown-document component (Angelo rejected the first implementation as misplaced). RichEditor takes os directly — the suggestionsProvider parameter goes away; mention(os) owns the full flow: watching the elements session, explicit index build on login (os.buildSearchIndex(profile)), ref→label mapping via os.store.get(ref). The provider abstraction is dropped. Session handling follows pos-navigation's pattern (watching the elements session store) — core keeps buildSearchIndex(profile) explicit and does NOT build the index on session appearance by itself; Angelo considered core-side building but chose to keep the explicit build (plan decision-05 stands). The first attempt's non-blocking design survives: nothing awaits os or index availability, suggestions are [] until the index is ready. SUPERSEDED (2026-10-14, decision-05): session handling moves into core entirely — the demand API removes the extension-side session watch and the explicit build; see scope-05 and task-07." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T20:07:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-context-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Task reshaped from the dissolved 'Search results carry labels' formulation during planning (2026-10-14). User quotes: \"I do not like to plan too far ahead, but pick the next suitable thing to do that helps us into the direciton of the goal\" (slice selection); \"i think we need to get a Thing from the store then for that ref\" (label resolution); \"do we need the score anywhere?\" (score: nothing consumes it); the reshape itself (no core change, Things built in the elements glue) was confirmed without an exactly quotable statement, scope choice: all the way working in one slice. An earlier TDD attempt of the {uri, label} result shape was fully reverted; the resulting ref→Thing design supersedes it.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T19:26:26Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-decision-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Search results stay ref-only lunr hits — SearchIndex/SearchGateway keep their public shape, core untouched. Labels resolve consumer-side: the label triples live in the label-index documents already fetched by buildSearchIndex, so os.store.get(ref) → Thing.label() resolves synchronously without extra fetches (pos-navigation already renders pos-rich-link uri=ref the same way). User: \"i think we need to get a Thing from the store then for that ref\". Supersedes the deferred item task-01 outOfScope-04 (result shape ref -> {uri, label}).";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T19:26:26Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-decision-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Things are built in the elements glue, not in core — user confirmed this reshape during planning (2026-10-14), scope chosen as 'all the way working' in one slice. os access enters RichEditor/mention via an injected suggestionsProvider: pos-markdown-document subscribes pod-os:init, obtains the dedup'd cached index via os.buildSearchIndex(profile) and hands a (query) => [{id, label}] function into the RichEditor constructor. SUPERSEDED (2026-10-14, decision-04): os-backed logic lives in the mention extension itself; RichEditor takes os directly, no injected provider.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T19:26:26Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-decision-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "No result-shape rework around the lunr score: nothing in the repo consumes it (only two SearchIndex.spec ordering assertions); keeping raw hits means no decision needed. User asked: \"do we need the score anywhere?\".";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T19:26:26Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-scope-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "RichEditor: constructor accepts a suggestionsProvider (query => Promise<{id, label}[]>) and passes it to mention(); mention() re-registered; the 3 skipped registration tests in RichEditor.spec.tsx un-skipped and adapted to the injected provider.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T19:26:26Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-scope-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "pos-markdown-document: subscribes pod-os:init; after login awaits os.buildSearchIndex(profile) (dedup'd cache -> cheap) and builds the provider mapping refs -> os.store.get(ref) -> {id: ref, label: thing.label()}. SUPERSEDED (2026-10-14, decision-04): the component does not own os or session logic anymore — see scope-04.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T19:26:26Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-scope-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "items.ts (hardcoded Alice/Bob/Carol) is removed; pos-navigation stays untouched (pos-rich-link resolves labels itself); no changes in core at all.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T19:26:26Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-scope-04> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Per decision-04 (2026-10-14): RichEditor constructor takes os: PodOS (replacing the suggestionsProvider parameter); mention(os) internally watches the elements session (like pos-navigation), calls os.buildSearchIndex(profile) explicitly on login, and maps search refs to {id, label} via os.store.get(ref).label(). pos-markdown-document reduces to pure wiring: obtains os via pod-os:init and passes it into the RichEditor constructor. index.spec.ts adapts to the new mention(os) signature; the SuggestionsProvider type is removed from rich-editor.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T20:07:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-verification-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "RichEditor.spec.tsx green with mention() re-registered and the 3 tests un-skipped; pos-mention-menu spec green; core suites untouched and green. Wallaby is available in the LLM sandbox (verified 2026-10-14 with core + pos-navigation suites) — this supersedes the older note that wallaby runs are user-side only.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T19:26:26Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-06-fallback-create-things-on-the-fly-goal-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "When the user types a mention label that matches nothing in the search index, the menu offers to create the thing and insert the mention for it. Created things stay unindexed — findability is deliberately left to the existing make-findable flow later.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T19:31:55Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-06-fallback-create-things-on-the-fly-outOfScope-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Adding the created thing to the label index (make-findable) is out of scope for now — creation only (user: \"without make findable for now, only creation\", 2026-10-14).";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T19:34:23Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-06-fallback-create-things-on-the-fly-context-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Slice-level 'how' (menu UI, thing-creation details, where/how the thing is stored, permissions) is deliberately not planned ahead; to be worked out when this task is picked up after task-05. The task stays in draft until planned through. Definition and stance recorded plan-level in decision-15.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T19:31:55Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-plan-decision-15> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Mention fallback defined and scoped: fallback = what the mention menu offers when a typed label matches nothing in the search index. Design space: (a) empty menu, nothing insertable (pos-navigation's behavior, search-only); (b) URI-paste escape hatch for existing-but-unindexed things; (c) create on the fly (mention menu offers to create the unindexed thing; make-findable deliberately excluded for now). User chose (c), refined to creation-only: recorded as draft follow-up task-06, depending on task-05; until it lands the search-only behavior (a) applies. This supersedes the out-of-scope ruling (decision-13; the former plan-level outOfScope entry was removed): the mention feature is back in scope — task-05 = suggestions provider + re-enable + un-skip, task-06 = fallback.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T19:31:55Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-plan-context-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Human topic (verbatim): \"instead of hard-coded items in RichEditor markdown mentions, i want to have a full text search from the search index, same as in pos-navigation\".";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-plan-context-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Terminology: 'full text search' is a mislabel — the index covers labels and URIs only, not document content. The mentions feature wants label search over findable things. Keeping scope as label search. (implicitly)";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>, <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-plan-context-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "User framing (verbatim): \"For sure we need a refactoring first and we should plan this now before diving deeper into the mentions feature. the question is where to build the search index and whether we need to 'globalize' it\".";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-plan-decision-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Move search into core. User: \"I think it makes sense to move it into core, since it is not a UI feature? even cli apps could make use of the search?\"";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-plan-decision-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Core owns lifecycle (option A-full, LLM inference from the user's core argument + headless-first choice): PodOS holds a SearchIndexService, built lazily when first consumer expresses need, shared thereafter; cleared on logout; updated internally by addToLabelIndex / createDefaultLabelIndex.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-plan-decision-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Build lazily on demand, not eagerly on login. User: \"i think it should be lazy, but not on first search, but as soon as a component needs it. like pos-navigation or the mention\". Demand signal: any consumer mount.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-plan-decision-04> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Keep warm until logout. User: \"keep warm.\" Invalidation on label change is an existing mechanism: pos-make-findable writes via core (os.addToLabelIndex / os.createDefaultLabelIndex) and only then echoes DOM events which pos-navigation consumes. With core-owned index, core rebuilds inside those gateway methods; DOM-event listeners become redundant.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-plan-decision-05> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Keep os.buildSearchIndex(profile) as the explicit demand call. User: \"why should we remove os.buildSearchIndex, i would still keep it explicit\". New semantics: de-duplicated ensure-build returning the shared instance; keyed on session profile; same-profile repeat calls are no-ops; profile change (re-login) rebuilds.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-plan-decision-06> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Core rebuilds internally on label changes (user confirmed): addToLabelIndex / createDefaultLabelIndex update the core-held index directly; DOM-event listeners in pos-navigation become redundant.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-plan-decision-07> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Remove pod-os:search:index-created/updated DOM events (user confirmed, breaking but contained — only in-repo consumers).";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-plan-decision-08> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Defer os-to-RichEditor bridge and mention fallback until after the refactor. User: \"focus on refactoring, we will discuss after that\" / \"later\".";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-plan-decision-09> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Headless-first design: core API must work without DOM; CLI/non-UI consumers usable from day one.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-plan-decision-10> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Scope guardrail: \"lets not add new things and focus on refactoring\" — pure deduplication/refactor of existing behavior, no new features.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-plan-decision-11> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Task-breakdown convention: plan = what (slice order/roadmap, plan-level decisions, plan-blocking open questions, task status); task files = how (code facts, slice-level scope, design sketches, test plans, slice-local open questions). LLM rule: before writing to plan ask 'does this change what we plan, or only how a planned item is done?' Only the latter goes to the task level. (clarified)";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-09"^^xsd:date.

<#entry-plan-decision-12> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Merge strategy for feat/markdown-mentions: disable the mention extension before merging (user: \"i would like to remove the mention extension from the editor. tests might break. i have no better idea to skip those then until the extension is back in\" / \"disable ext. skip affectedf tests\" / \"Skip via .skip\"). Unregister mention() in RichEditor.ts on the branch; the 3 registration-tied tests in RichEditor.spec.tsx get .skip treatment (user chose .skip over delete-and-restore); standalone tests keep running; mention rendering/serialization code (PosRichLinkMark, markdown syntax) stays on main inert; re-add path: when the search-based provider lands, the extension is re-registered and the 3 skipped tests un-skipped. Applied: disable commit made on feat/markdown-mentions, RichEditor suite green (39 passed / 3 skipped / 0 failed), LSP diagnostics clean; pending: commit plan-file move, then merge tip to main.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-plan-decision-13> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Scope ruling for the remaining plan: the mention feature is out of scope — this plan is only about the search refactoring. User: \"the mention should be out of scope, we are focusing on the search refactoring only here\". Consequently openQuestion-01 (os-to-RichEditor bridge) and openQuestion-02 (mention fallback) are no longer open in this plan. SUPERSEDED (2026-10-14): the mention feature is back in scope — task-05 (provider + re-enable) and task-06 (fallback), see decision-15.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T15:58:28Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-plan-outOfScope-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "[REMOVED 2026-10-14] The mentions feature in all its parts: search-based suggestion provider for RichEditor (os-to-RichEditor bridge), mention fallback for things not in the index, re-enabling the mention extension and un-skipping its 3 tests. User: \"the mention should be out of scope, we are focusing on the search refactoring only here\". All parts are back in scope — provider + re-enable/un-skip via task-05, fallback via task-06 (decision-15); the plan:outOfScope assertion was removed from the plan because such an assertion must reflect current scope, the history lives here and in decision-13/15.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T15:58:28Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-plan-option-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "A. Core-owned search service: PodOS holds a SearchIndex instance; lifecycle built on login, invalidated/rebuilt on label-index change events, cleared on logout; consumers call os.search(term) synchronously. + lunr and LabelIndex logic already live in core; single source of truth; one fetch, one rebuild. - core must know about session/login lifecycle or get an explicit initSearch(profile) call; introduces stateful lifetime into an otherwise stateless-ish facade; elements must still bridge os-to-RichEditor (RichEditor has no os reference; needs a suggestionsProvider callback injected at construction).";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-plan-option-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "B. Shared service in elements package: a tiny module in elements/src owns index lifecycle (subscribes session + index events once), exposes an observable / query function. Core API stays as-is. + core stays thin; consumers live in elements anyway; no core API surface change. - singleton module is hidden global state; harder to test; two search entry points (os.buildSearchIndex still exists) can drift.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-plan-option-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "C. Status quo pattern (per-component build): pos-markdown-document subscribes pod-os:init + session like pos-navigation and builds its own index. + least refactoring, proven pattern, testable in isolation. - N times label-index fetches and lunr rebuilds; staleness wiring duplicated per consumer; RichEditor still needs the bridge; with a third consumer this clearly breaks down.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-plan-note-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Middle path: lifecycle correctness (one owner of build/rebuild/clear, others just query) matters more than where the instance lives; both A and B can satisfy it; A puts the truth in core, B in elements.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-plan-note-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Exposure analysis for the merge decision: the hardcoded suggestion menu (Alice/Bob/Carol on localhost:3000) only appears when a user with edit permission enters edit mode and types '#'; view mode and stored mention markdown ([@ id=... label=...] rendered as pos-rich-link) don't touch items.ts. But elements is published and pos-document/pos-app-document-viewer pass editable through — downstream editors would see fake suggestions and could insert broken URIs.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-plan-decision-14> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Questions no longer open, converted to decisions: (1) os-to-RichEditor bridge design — dissolved: the mention feature is out of scope for this plan (decision-13); the bridge question moves with it to a future mentions plan. (2) Mention fallback for things not in the index — dissolved for the same reason. (3) Naming of core search service class — resolved: the SearchGateway itself holds the cache; no new service class was introduced, so there is nothing to name. (resolved 2026-10-14)";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T16:21:32Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-goal-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Repeated calls to os.buildSearchIndex(profile) with the same profile return the same cached SearchIndex instance instead of fetching label indexes and rebuilding every time.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-scope-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Cache only: no logout-clear, no DOM-event changes, no result-shape change.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-scope-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Same profile -> no-op; different profile -> rebuild. 'Same profile' means comparing profile.webId (not object identity).";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-scope-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "No in-flight dedup: concurrent first calls may each build; last writer wins. Accepted wart.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-scope-04> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Test security: new core spec pinning caching semantics; pos-navigation suite stays green. Wallaby runs are executed on the user's side (LLM sandbox cannot run wallaby).";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-verification-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "New unit spec: same webId twice -> same SearchIndex instance (toBe), one fetchAll call; different webId -> new instance, second fetch; empty-profile path -> empty SearchIndex, cached (same instance on repeat). (from decisions)";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>, <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-outOfScope-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Clearing cached index on logout -> creates a known stale cross-user index window (re-login as another user serves the previous user's label index until a rebuild is triggered). Flagged as privacy-adjacent; superseded by task-02's plain-cache + logout-clear.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-outOfScope-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Internal rebuild on addToLabelIndex / createDefaultLabelIndex (task-02).";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-outOfScope-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Removal of pod-os:search:index-created/updated DOM events (tasks 03/04).";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-outOfScope-04> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Result shape {ref} -> {uri, label}.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-outOfScope-05> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "os-to-RichEditor bridge, mention fallback.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-decision-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Cache placement resolved: inside SearchGateway (it already owns build logic).";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-decision-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Event-triggered rebuild bypassed by cache is not an issue: SearchIndex.rebuild() never goes through os.buildSearchIndex; pos-navigation's rebuildSearchIndex() calls SearchIndex.rebuild() directly, re-reading label indexes from the store in place.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-decision-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Stale cross-user index on re-login is not an issue: the cache is keyed by webId, so login as a different user is a cache miss and triggers a fresh build; pos-navigation additionally clears its index on logout.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-decision-04> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Unit tests suffice for the cache. Angelo challenged integration tests: \"why do we need integration tests, i think unit would be enough for the caching feature\". Caching semantics (memoization by webId) are pure logic, tested unit-style in SearchGateway.spec.ts with a fake Store. The duplicated describe(\"caching\") block was removed from SearchGateway.integration.spec.ts; the original build-search-index integration tests remain (they cover fetch -> parse -> LabelIndex -> SearchIndex wiring on first build). Accepted trade-off: no test asserts that the memoized index still searches correctly (wiring is covered by the non-cached integration tests). The extracted pure cache class (SearchIndexCache) was NOT taken — fake-store unit tests on SearchGateway are sufficient.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-09"^^xsd:date.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-decision-05> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Implementation review (Angelo, 2026-10-09): the duplicated cache-write/return in the two branches was consolidated; the let assignment was replaced by a private buildIndex() helper with an early return for the empty-profile path.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-09"^^xsd:date.

<#entry-task-01-cache-search-index-in-core-note-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Task superseded in parts by task-02 (plain cache, no webId keying; logout-clear added there). Open questions from this task were all resolved.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-goal-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "With a cache present, addToLabelIndex rebuilds the cached index in place and createDefaultLabelIndex recreates it, so core owns index freshness. Both updates are awaited before the method resolves — callers get a freshness guarantee (unlike the pre-01 event timing, which was racy). (from post-task-01 discussion)";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-context-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Code facts: Store.get(uri) returns a fresh wrapper but reads live from the shared rdflib store; LabelIndex.getIndexedItems() re-reads the store, so SearchIndex.rebuild() sees statements written after build time — as long as the label-index document set is unchanged. SearchIndex privately holds the LabelIndex[] captured at construction. rebuild() is called in exactly two places today: the SearchIndex constructor and pos-navigation's pod-os:search:index-updated listener. Pre-01 semantics: the index-updated path never refetched (shared store already had the new triples); the index-created path called buildSearchIndex, which refetched all label indexes.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-context-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Regression from task-01 (commit 47c1360a): the create-default-index flow broke — post-01 the buildSearchIndex call is a cache hit (same webId) so a stale instance is returned, and a rebuild over the captured (possibly empty) LabelIndex[] never includes the new document. User named the underlying issue: the cached SearchIndex contains a list of all label indexes, so a new index document requires more than rebuild() — it requires building the cached index anew; rebuild() naming is confusing for that. (user confirmed)";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-context-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Ordering challenge: if the real goal is re-enabling the mention extension (disabled for the merge), the shortest path is result-shape + bridge with clean-up afterwards; if the goal is 'core is the single source of search truth first', this task comes first. Plan leans refactoring-first; user chose this task.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>, <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-decision-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Plain cache, no webId keying. User challenged the webId key from task-01: \"why do we need the cache by web id at all? only one user is logged in at a time and the cache needs to be cleared on logout\". The gateway holds one optional SearchIndex; the {webId, index} tuple and its comparison logic are removed (small refactor of task-01's cache, no new functionality).";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-decision-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Cache cleared on logout — follows from the same quote; implementation goes through core's existing session subscription. Task-01's resolved open question ('cross-user staleness handled by webId keying') is thereby superseded.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-decision-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "No cache -> no-op on write paths: \"if nothing cached nothing needs to be rebuilt -> noop\". Write paths never build an index.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-decision-04> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Method-per-operation. User challenged the discriminator options: \"why so complicated. recreation right now is only when default index is created\". addToLabelIndex -> cache exists -> rebuild() (document set unchanged; captured LabelIndex objects read the new triples live from the store). createDefaultLabelIndex -> cache exists -> recreate: build a fresh SearchIndex from the current profile.getPrivateLabelIndexes() (the solid:privateLabelIndex triple is already in the local rdflib store when the subsequent add runs). Supersedes the earlier interim decision 'only addToLabelIndex touches the cache'.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-decision-05> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Pure refactor, no new functionality: the moved trigger is the existing pos-navigation index-updated rebuild; recreation restores pre-01 index-created refetch semantics in deterministic form (bug fix, not new behavior). Core-only slice: pos-navigation untouched; its index-updated listener becomes a harmless duplicate rebuild of the same object.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-verification-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Unit tests (fake Store, style of task-01): buildSearchIndex twice -> same instance; after logout-simulation (cache cleared) -> next call builds again. addToLabelIndex with no cache -> store write happens, fetchAll not called, no rebuild. addToLabelIndex with cache -> same instance (toBe), search() finds the added item, no refetch of label indexes. createDefaultLabelIndex with cache -> cache is a new instance, search() finds an item added to the new index afterwards (via subsequent addToLabelIndex in the same test). createDefaultLabelIndex with no cache -> no build. Awaiting: promise from addToLabelIndex resolves only after the cache update. Logout-clear: unit-testable via the session subject, covered at the level the existing flagAuthorizationMetadata tap is covered.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-verification-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Wallaby run (user side): core suite + pos-navigation suite green.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-scope-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "SearchGateway: replace private cached? {webId, index} with private cached? SearchIndex; buildSearchIndex(profile) drops the webId comparison — cache exists -> return it, else build (empty-profile path still caches an empty index).";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-scope-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "SearchGateway.addToLabelIndex(thing, labelIndex): await store.executeUpdate(...), then if (this.cached) { this.cached.rebuild(); }.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-scope-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "SearchGateway.createDefaultLabelIndex(profile): after executeUpdate and returning the LabelIndex, if this.cached exists -> recreate: this.cached = await this.buildIndex(profile.getPrivateLabelIndexes()) — refetches the label-index documents (including the new one) and constructs a fresh SearchIndex (reuses the existing private buildIndex helper).";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-scope-04> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "PodOS: in the session subscription (alongside flagAuthorizationMetadata()), clear the gateway's cache when the session ends.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-note-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Open question 1 (webId scoping/discriminator) dissolved by the plain-cache + method-per-operation decisions.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-note-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Open question 2 (session-clear hook shape), resolved direction: the existing flagAuthorizationMetaDataOnSessionChange tap could be used 'but should probably be renamed' since it would then do more than flag authorization metadata; proposal for the logout-clear slice: rename to handleSessionChange(), body delegates to named private reactions (store.flagAuthorizationMetadata(), later searchGateway.clear()). Exact naming decided when that slice is planned.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-note-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Open question 3 (DOM-event removal): decided — 'the breaking change is still acceptable'; remove pod-os:search:index-created/updated in a slice after this task. Analysis: the deprecate-while-emitting alternative seems moot given core owns index freshness after this task.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-09"^^xsd:date.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-note-04> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Open question 4 (filesToCreate: [] in createDefaultLabelIndex): the returned operation lists no files to create even though the target file may not exist yet (presumably the solid server creates it on PUT — to verify). Does not affect gateway logic; noted.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-note-05> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Open question 5 (logout-clear timing vs in-flight build): if buildSearchIndex is mid-flight during logout, the clear must not be overwritten by the completing build (task-01 accepted 'no in-flight dedup'; the clear adds a stale-write race). Accepted as-is: wart stands, no code change.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>, <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-10"^^xsd:date.

<#entry-task-02-recreate-search-index-on-label-update-note-06> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Post-implementation review: two-axis LLM review ran 2026-10-10; findings triaged and not acted on. The profile-staleness concern was retracted on re-verification (getPrivateLabelIndexes() reads live from the rdflib store and createDefaultLabelIndex's update operations already insert the solid:privateLabelIndex triple before the recreate runs); the remaining findings were test-assertion nits and style notes. Implemented via commits e82ee88a..9c14f84b.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>, <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>.

<#entry-task-03-remove-search-dom-events-goal-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "The pod-os:search:index-created/updated DOM events and their listeners are gone; core's internal cache updates (task-02) are the sole mechanism keeping search indexes fresh.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T15:58:28Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-03-remove-search-dom-events-scope-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "pos-make-findable: remove the two @Event emitters (indexUpdatedEmitter, indexCreatedEmitter) and the emits in onClick() and onSelect().";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T15:58:28Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-03-remove-search-dom-events-scope-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "pos-navigation: drop the two @Listen decorators (pod-os:search:index-created on buildSearchIndex, pod-os:search:index-updated on rebuildSearchIndex). Keep the buildSearchIndex method — the session subscriber's login branch already calls it. Remove rebuildSearchIndex() entirely: the searchIndex it holds is core's shared cached instance, which core rebuilds in place (task-02), so the component reference stays fresh without any listener.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T15:58:28Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-03-remove-search-dom-events-scope-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Update the affected specs: pos-navigation.spec.tsx (the two tests dispatching pod-os:search:index-created/updated at lines ~505/520), pos-make-findable.spec.tsx (the three listener assertions at lines ~69/204/461).";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T15:58:28Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-03-remove-search-dom-events-verification-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "pos-navigation suite green without the event-dispatch tests (index still built on login via session subscription; search results reflect core-side rebuilds). pos-make-findable suite green without event assertions (addToLabelIndex / createDefaultLabelIndex still resolve and update isIndexed). Wallaby runs are executed on the user's side.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T15:58:28Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-03-remove-search-dom-events-decision-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "No replacement trigger needed for pos-navigation: its session subscription already calls buildSearchIndex when isLoggedIn becomes true (the @Listen decorator on that same method was an additional path). Index freshness after the removal comes from core rebuilding the shared cached instance in place, so the component's searchIndex reference sees the updates.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T15:58:28Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-03-remove-search-dom-events-note-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Bug report (user, after merge): with a user who has no label index at all, the first 'make findable' click leaves pos-navigation searching an empty index — the newly created index never reaches it. Diagnosis: the task-03 scope-02 assumption 'core rebuilds the shared cached instance in place, so the component reference stays fresh' only holds for addToLabelIndex (cached.rebuild()). createDefaultLabelIndex REPLACES this.cached with a fresh SearchIndex built from the updated label-index document list (task-02 scope-03). Sequence: login builds and caches an empty SearchIndex; user clicks make-findable with no existing index; createDefaultLabelIndex swaps the cache to a new instance; addToLabelIndex then rebuilds the NEW instance; pos-navigation still holds the OLD empty one and its search() returns nothing. Pre-task-03 the pod-os:search:index-created event triggered a buildSearchIndex call in pos-navigation, which masked this reference invalidation (the de-duplication made the create path return the updated cached instance).";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>, <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T17:53:21Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-03-remove-search-dom-events-openQuestion-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "How to fix the create-path reference invalidation without re-adding DOM events? Candidate A: SearchGateway.createDefaultLabelIndex updates the cached SearchIndex in place (e.g. SearchIndex.setLabelIndexes(labelIndexes) assigning the new LabelIndex[] and rebuilding) so all consumers keep holding a live reference. Candidate B: keep cache replacement and re-introduce a component-side re-fetch trigger (contra: contradicts task-03's decision-01). A also amends task-02 scope-03's formulation 'this.cached = await this.buildIndex(...)'. Affected test: SearchGateway.spec 'recreates the cached search index including the new label index document' asserts not.toBe(cachedIndex) and would flip to toBe; pos-navigation.spec needs a regression test: build index while profile has no label indexes, then createDefaultLabelIndex, then search must find the added thing. RESOLVED (2026-10-14): candidate A chosen in refined form — rebuild(labelIndexes?) instead of setLabelIndexes(); see task-04 decision-01. Candidate B rejected (contradicts task-03 decision-01).";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T17:53:21Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-04-fix-cache-reference-invalidation-goal-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "All consumers holding the shared cached SearchIndex keep a live reference across BOTH label-index write paths — pos-navigation's search finds things added via the make-findable flow even when the user had no label index at login.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T18:05:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-04-fix-cache-reference-invalidation-decision-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Fix A with optional-parameter variant: SearchIndex.rebuild(labelIndexes?) accepts an optional LabelIndex[] replacing the captured list before rebuilding; SearchGateway.createDefaultLabelIndex updates the cached instance in place via this.cached.rebuild(await this.resolveLabelIndexes(profile.getPrivateLabelIndexes())) instead of replacing this.cached (Angelo: \"we could also pass optional labelindexes to rebuild to update them\"). Supersedes task-02 scope-03's this.cached = await this.buildIndex(...) formulation and the setLabelIndexes() variant of task-03 openQuestion-01 candidate A; both write paths now update the same cached instance. No DOM events, no notification API for now (data freshness only; already-rendered suggestions refresh on next input).";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T18:10:57Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-04-fix-cache-reference-invalidation-verification-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Implemented TDD via wallaby, two cycles: (1) SearchIndex.spec 'replaces the label indexes when new ones are passed and finds their items' red, then rebuild(labelIndexes?) green. (2) SearchGateway.spec 'recreates the cached search index including the new label index document' flipped not.toBe -> toBe, red, then in-place createDefaultLabelIndex green. Separate refactor commit dropped the redundant empty short-circuit in buildIndex. All 36 tests green via wallaby; typecheck clean. Committed 3edab696, 5edde550, 1570f8fd. Scoping: the planned pos-navigation regression test (cycle 3) was dropped — the gateway-level tests fully pin the behavior (same instance, fresh search results, both label-index documents fetched), so a component test would only duplicate the core contract.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>, <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T18:41:34Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-04-fix-cache-reference-invalidation-note-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Task spun off from task-03's bug report (note-01) and open question (openQuestion-01). Fix candidates are undecided: A (createDefaultLabelIndex updates the cached SearchIndex in place via SearchIndex.setLabelIndexes) vs B (keep cache replacement, re-introduce a component-side re-fetch trigger — contradicts task-03 decision-01). Decision pending with Angelo; see task-03 openQuestion-01 for details and affected tests. RESOLVED: see decision-01 and task-03 openQuestion-01.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T18:05:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.

<#entry-task-04-fix-cache-reference-invalidation-note-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Process note: refactoring must only happen in a verified green state. Angelo: \"it is fine to do the refactoring in the same commit, as long as it happens only when all tests are green\". On whether the refactor step should be a separate commit (Angelo: \"do you think it would be better to make the refactoring step a separate commit?\"), the separate-commit style was agreed as preferred (structurally enforces the green checkpoint); the tdd-task prompt was updated with this rule. Scoping decisions (Angelo: \"1. drop it 2. update it 3. captured is ok\"): the planned pos-navigation regression test (cycle 3) is omitted — the gateway-level tests fully pin the behavior (same instance, fresh search results, both label-index documents fetched), so a component test would only duplicate the core contract; the plan status update was requested; the 'captured' local variable in SearchIndex.rebuild (needed because the lunr callback rebinds this) stays as-is.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-14T18:41:34Z"^^xsd:dateTime.
